<!--
  SecretPrinter.Listen6.csproj

  Written by Claude (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 5) at the direction of
  Edwin West, 2026-09-13, for the SecretPrinter project. Reviewed by a human
  before merge.

  The two mentions of SecretPrinter.Respond6 below updated by Claude (Anthropic
  model, Claude Opus 5.5) at the direction of Edwin West, 2026-10-02, when that
  tool was deleted. Comments only. Reviewed by a human before merge.

  A receive-only diagnostic, the IPv6 counterpart of SecretPrinter.Listen. It
  answers one question: does IPV6_PKTINFO report a usable arrival interface
  index on this platform? REQ-ADV-020 depends on the answer. The result is
  recorded in docs/findings/2026-09-13-ipv6-pktinfo-arrival.md.

  Deliberately carries no Requirement markers, for the same reason as
  SecretPrinter.Respond: the requirements in README.md describe the service. A
  marker here would make the coverage matrix report a service behaviour when
  what exists is a measurement of the operating system.

  No project references and no NuGet packages. The socket configuration is
  written out in full rather than shared with SecretPrinter.Mdns, so that the
  thing being measured cannot silently change when the product changes. That is
  duplication on purpose; the correspondence is listed in the Program.cs header
  for a reader to check.

  This project is not scheduled for deletion. SecretPrinter.Respond6 was, and
  was deleted on 2026-10-02 (the last commit that holds it is a10087d). This
  one measures a property of the operating system, which is worth re-checking
  on a new machine, a new Windows build, or a new adapter.

  Common build settings, including the target framework, come from
  Directory.Build.props at the repository root and are not restated here.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>SecretPrinter.Listen6</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>SecretPrinter.Listen6</AssemblyName>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
    <!-- Diagnostic only: never packed, never signed, never released. -->
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
